WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
The Census Bureau groups the
US states into four regions:

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.510
Northeast, Midwest, South and West.

3
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.110
That gives the Midwest
one tidy outline on a map.

4
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.010
Now ask people to draw
the Midwest themselves.

5
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:15.930
The outlines don't match.

6
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.410
So where does the Midwest really end?

7
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.470
Should the government draw one line?

8
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.210
Should each state decide?

9
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.710
In this mission, you'll test
what makes an area a region,

10
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.330
from a pizza delivery zone
to a whole metro area.

11
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.970
Then you'll see what a sharp
line on a map can hide.

12
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.650
Your mission: decide
where the Midwest ends,

13
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.720
and who gets to decide.
